Speak (text to speech), Clone (a voice from a short recording, with consent), Design (a voice from words), Transcribe
(text, SRT, VTT, speaker labels), a voice library shared by everything, Audiobooks and Video dubbing (a queue on disk
that carries on after a restart or a game), and an OpenAI-compatible speech API for the Hearth AI Command Center and
other apps. Written for Hearth (no code from other voice studios).

  hearth-voice-studio serve                the page and the API (hearth-voice-studio.service through hearth-home-server
                                           ai-run voicestudio, in the engines' own venv), port 8890, on 127.0.0.1 and
                                           this PC's Tailscale address only
  hearth-voice-studio status               JSON for Settings: installed, engines, PIN, API key set, addresses
  hearth-voice-studio set KEY VALUE        language (a code or auto), voice (a voice id or ''), translateModel (an
                                           Ollama model or ''), speakerLabels (on|off)
  hearth-voice-studio pin-set              the page's PIN on stdin (HEARTH_INPUT; 4-12 digits; only its hash is kept)
  hearth-voice-studio pin-clear            no PIN of its own (Server mode's PIN then works, if one is set)
  hearth-voice-studio key-show             the API key (made the first time; for the Command Center)
  hearth-voice-studio key-new              a new API key (the old one stops working)
  hearth-voice-studio install-job          the install itself (hearth-home-server studio-install runs it in its own unit)
  hearth-voice-studio remove [voices sure] the engines and downloaded models go; your voices and finished work stay
                                           unless you confirmed twice
  hearth-voice-studio mock-serve [PORT]    the page with stand-in engines (tests and CI screenshots only)

Your choices: ~/.config/nimbus/voice-studio.json through hearth_settings_io (only the key you change; atomic, .bak,
merged under the lock; defaults filled in when read, never saved). State, never settings: the PIN's hash, the page's
sign-ins and the API key (~/.local/state/nimbus/voice-studio-web.json, 0600). Your voices, the queue and finished work:
~/.local/share/nimbus/voice-studio (voices/, jobs/), with the engines' venv and models beside them (venv/, models/).
Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1.
